candidates.evidence_quote:
•an increase of $700 million in fiber broadband revenue primarily due to the inclusion of Frontier results;
•an increase of $190 million related to growth in non-retail service revenue; and
•a decrease of $299 million in postpaid revenue primarily related to the amortization of wireless equipment sales promotions and acquisition related discounts

•an increase of $201 million and $465 million, respectively, in personnel costs mainly driven by an increase in employee headcount following the acquisition of Frontier;
•an increase of $79 million and $229 million, respectively, in digital content costs primarily associated with an increase in subscriptions through plan offerings and the inclusion of Frontier results, partially offset by a decrease in traditional linear content costs related to lower Fios video volumes; and
•an increase of $56 million and $181 million, respectively, in building and facility costs
